{
  "requirement": "The SDK presents node inputs using the returned value's `NodeContents::format`\nunder {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`.\nIts text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.\n\n```rust,ignore\nlet contents = domain.node_content(&node_id)?;\nlet text = contents.format();\n```\n\nLoading and fallible preparation occur in `Domain::node_content` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content`. For inputs queued on an ask\nbuilder, these failures return `ValidationError::Graph`. During a `read_node`\ntool call, they are returned to the agent as a tool error, so it can continue\nand recover.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `judge.rendering`.\n\n**1. Inputs are presented through `NodeContents::format`.**\n- In `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/agent.rs`, the test memory domain stores the fingerprint text in `Content.0` and the `format()` output in `Content.1`. The `Content` impl's `format` returns `Content.1`. The `distinct_pages` formatter makes the formatted text differ from the fingerprint: it produces `ALPHA-CONTENTS:source` repeated many times, while the fingerprint is just `source`.\n- `validator_agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces` uses `distinct_pages`. The `ParallelConversations` provider asserts that the first request's history contains the formatted `ALPHA-CONTENTS` or `BETA-CONTENTS` marker. It also asserts that later `get_node_page` results contain the right marker and none from the other conversation. The same test asserts that the recorded dependency fingerprints are the plain `\"source\"`. A presenter that sent the fingerprint instead of `format()` would therefore fail.\n- `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` checks which inputs are delivered, in what order, with repeats, and that each is read once (`reads == [1, 3, 2, 3, 1]`).\n- `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` and `behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer` check the delivered text. The latter also checks input order in the delivered message.\n\n**2. Text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.**\n- `identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot` in `contracts.rs` mutates the underlying content after the read. It then asserts that `format()` still returns `\"before\"`, that `fingerprint()` equals the snapshot's fingerprint, and that only one read occurred.\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` shows that formatting uses the supplied snapshot without re-reading the source.\n\n**3. Failures return the right error for each path.**\n- For queued builder inputs, `queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation` forces a read failure (`fail_read`) and a preparation failure (`fail_prepare`). It asserts `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"read\"))` and `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"render\"))`. It also asserts that no dependency is recorded and that the agent is never invoked.\n- For `read_node` tool calls, `node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents` makes the formatter or preparation fail. It asserts that the agent receives a tool result with `is_error` set, named `read_node`, carrying the error text. It then asserts that the agent continues to a second request and submits. It also asserts that no dependency is recorded for undelivered contents.\n\nThe remaining marked tests reference this requirement, but they only exercise it incidentally. They are `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` and `authoring_keeps_the_prepared_subject_snapshot_and_concrete_version`.\n\nThe `fingerprint_content` and `fingerprint_content.format` requirements are cited context. The \"no further reads or fallible preparation in format\" obligation belongs to them.\n\nI found no untested obligation and no inadequate assertion. No `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "55ef6d58a89754ddd0ee9008bea5872fcc366388e4d0f41325533730a08c2e28",
